    "title": "Netflix films scenes for new movie at Livingston deli - NewsBreak",
    "text": "A Livingston deli is going Hollywood. Nana’s Deli served as a filming location for a new Netflix movie reportedly involving Adam Sandler. It reopened on Wednesday after several days of filming. Nana’s Deli has been in business for more than 40 years. MORE: Netflix releases trailer for ‘Happy Gilmore 2’ “My dad started the business…The movie has been amazing for us already. We opened today. We’ve had hundreds of calls, almost a thousand emails, tons of people contacting us. It’s amazing for New Jersey and just our business,” says Jason Dworkin, of Nana’s Deli. New Jersey is no stranger to movie productions. Sandler shot many scenes for “Happy Gilmore 2” across the state.",
